    <item>
      <title>Getting Familiar</title>
      <link>https://example.org/docs/getting-started/getting-familar/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>https://example.org/docs/getting-started/getting-familar/</guid>
      <description>
        
        
        &lt;p&gt;After installtion, now we need to get familar with Aurora.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;hx:overflow-x-auto hx:mt-6 hx:flex hx:flex-col hx:rounded-lg hx:border hx:py-4 hx:px-4 hx:border-gray-200 hx:contrast-more:border-current hx:contrast-more:dark:border-current hx:border-purple-200 hx:bg-purple-100 hx:text-purple-900 hx:dark:border-purple-200/30 hx:dark:bg-purple-900/30 hx:dark:text-purple-200&#34;&gt;
  &lt;p class=&#34;hx:flex hx:items-center hx:font-medium&#34;&gt;&lt;svg height=16px class=&#34;hx:inline-block hx:align-middle hx:mr-2&#34; xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34; d=&#34;M13 16h-1v-4h-1m1-4h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;Important&lt;/p&gt;

  &lt;div class=&#34;hx:w-full hx:min-w-0 hx:leading-7&#34;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;hx:mt-6 hx:leading-7 hx:first:mt-0&#34;&gt;&lt;p&gt;After installation please restart your session&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After your first login, you should see &lt;code&gt;Aurora&#39;s Welcome app&lt;/code&gt;. It will welcome you to the system everytime you log in.
&lt;img src=&#34;../images/welcome_app.png&#34; alt=&#34;Welcome app&#34;  loading=&#34;lazy&#34; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a gtk app. You can close this welcome app by pressing &lt;code&gt;ESCAPE&lt;/code&gt; key.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;hx:overflow-x-auto hx:mt-6 hx:flex hx:flex-col hx:rounded-lg hx:border hx:py-4 hx:px-4 hx:border-gray-200 hx:contrast-more:border-current hx:contrast-more:dark:border-current hx:border-purple-200 hx:bg-purple-100 hx:text-purple-900 hx:dark:border-purple-200/30 hx:dark:bg-purple-900/30 hx:dark:text-purple-200&#34;&gt;
  &lt;p class=&#34;hx:flex hx:items-center hx:font-medium&#34;&gt;&lt;svg height=16px class=&#34;hx:inline-block hx:align-middle hx:mr-2&#34; xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34; d=&#34;M13 16h-1v-4h-1m1-4h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;Important&lt;/p&gt;

  &lt;div class=&#34;hx:w-full hx:min-w-0 hx:leading-7&#34;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;hx:mt-6 hx:leading-7 hx:first:mt-0&#34;&gt;&lt;p&gt;All Aurora&amp;rsquo;s custom gui apps can be closed using &lt;code&gt;ESCAPE&lt;/code&gt; key&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Keybinds help&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;keybinds-help&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#keybinds-help&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;As you can see, you need to know some keybinds to get familiar. Press &lt;code&gt;SUPER + H&lt;/code&gt; to launch keybinds help app. It will guide you with keybinds.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;hx:overflow-x-auto hx:mt-6 hx:flex hx:flex-col hx:rounded-lg hx:border hx:py-4 hx:px-4 hx:border-gray-200 hx:contrast-more:border-current hx:contrast-more:dark:border-current hx:border-purple-200 hx:bg-purple-100 hx:text-purple-900 hx:dark:border-purple-200/30 hx:dark:bg-purple-900/30 hx:dark:text-purple-200&#34;&gt;
  &lt;p class=&#34;hx:flex hx:items-center hx:font-medium&#34;&gt;&lt;svg height=16px class=&#34;hx:inline-block hx:align-middle hx:mr-2&#34; xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34; d=&#34;M13 16h-1v-4h-1m1-4h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;Important&lt;/p&gt;

  &lt;div class=&#34;hx:w-full hx:min-w-0 hx:leading-7&#34;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;hx:mt-6 hx:leading-7 hx:first:mt-0&#34;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Super key mean &lt;code&gt;Window&lt;/code&gt; key on your keyboard&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Some crucial keybinds&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;some-crucial-keybinds&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#some-crucial-keybinds&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;table&gt;
  &lt;thead&gt;
      &lt;tr&gt;
          &lt;th style=&#34;text-align: left&#34;&gt;Keybind&lt;/th&gt;
          &lt;th style=&#34;text-align: left&#34;&gt;Action&lt;/th&gt;
      &lt;/tr&gt;
  &lt;/thead&gt;
  &lt;tbody&gt;
      &lt;tr&gt;
          &lt;td style=&#34;text-align: left&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;SUPER + H&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
          &lt;td style=&#34;text-align: left&#34;&gt;To open the keybinds help app&lt;/td&gt;
      &lt;/tr&gt;
      &lt;tr&gt;
          &lt;td style=&#34;text-align: left&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;SUPER + R&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
          &lt;td style=&#34;text-align: left&#34;&gt;to launch app launcher&lt;/td&gt;
      &lt;/tr&gt;
      &lt;tr&gt;
          &lt;td style=&#34;text-align: left&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;SUPER + Q&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
          &lt;td style=&#34;text-align: left&#34;&gt;To launch default terminal&lt;/td&gt;
      &lt;/tr&gt;
      &lt;tr&gt;
          &lt;td style=&#34;text-align: left&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;SUPER + C&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
          &lt;td style=&#34;text-align: left&#34;&gt;To close active window&lt;/td&gt;
      &lt;/tr&gt;
  &lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are new to Hyprland, you may wonder what&amp;rsquo;s that in the top. It&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;Waybar&lt;/code&gt;. It is very useful for Hyprland users.  You can see currently it shows you the workspaces number (which is 10 in Aurora by default). It also shows the current window title, clock (you can see calender by hovering it). Also volume level and battery percentage and wifi and bluetooth menu, etc.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can view Aurora&amp;rsquo;s settings by pressing &lt;code&gt;SUPER + SHIFT + Z&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;hx:overflow-x-auto hx:mt-6 hx:flex hx:flex-col hx:rounded-lg hx:border hx:py-4 hx:px-4 hx:border-gray-200 hx:contrast-more:border-current hx:contrast-more:dark:border-current hx:border-purple-200 hx:bg-purple-100 hx:text-purple-900 hx:dark:border-purple-200/30 hx:dark:bg-purple-900/30 hx:dark:text-purple-200&#34;&gt;
  &lt;p class=&#34;hx:flex hx:items-center hx:font-medium&#34;&gt;&lt;svg height=16px class=&#34;hx:inline-block hx:align-middle hx:mr-2&#34; xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34; d=&#34;M13 16h-1v-4h-1m1-4h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z&#34;/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;Important&lt;/p&gt;

  &lt;div class=&#34;hx:w-full hx:min-w-0 hx:leading-7&#34;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;hx:mt-6 hx:leading-7 hx:first:mt-0&#34;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;Super&lt;/code&gt; key means the &lt;code&gt;Window&lt;/code&gt; key in your keyboard&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

      </description>
    </item>
    
